+# The Eight Sacred Forces
+
+**Foundations 0.1** · `codex/01-foundations/eight-forces.md`
+
+The forces are the eight ways the flow can hold itself — the eight marks the First Weaver drew out of the water (told in `first-flow.md`). A force is not a god, an element, or a quality. It is a **posture of the flow**: a way motion can keep moving while leaving a mark.
+
+How to read each profile below:
+
+- **First mark** — how the force was drawn, in one line
+- **Character** — how the force behaves in the weave
+- **Gift** — what the force gives the world
+- **Shadow** — the force's excess; what goes wrong under it
+- **Crossing** — the pairing the force most loves, and what their crossing makes
+- **In the weave** — where the force lives (words of the dictionary)
+- **Its voice** — the force's manner in ritual speech
+- **In the language** — prefix and representative words
+
+---
+
+## The Wheel of Flow
+
+The eight do not sit still. They form a **wheel** — the order in which the flow passes through itself and comes home. Each force, carried to its fullness, becomes the next:
+
+```
+                AEL
+             (the Thaw)
+              /      \
+           RAV        MOR
+       (the Deep)  (the Sowing)
+            |          |
+           KEL        THAL
+        (the Far    (the Setting)
+          Night)         |
+            |           VUR
+           LUM      (the Ripening)
+        (the        \      /
+          Clearing)   SYR
+               (the Scattering)
+```
+
+Clockwise from the top: **Ael → Mor → Thal → Vur → Syr → Lum → Kel → Rav** → back to Ael.
+
+The wheel in words:
+
+| From | Becomes | Why |
+|------|---------|-----|
+| **Ael** → | **Mor** | flow, full of itself, nourishes — the root is flow that learned to reach |
+| **Mor** → | **Thal** | roots press into stone — growth, completed, is endurance |
+| **Thal** → | **Vur** | stone, held to its fullness, heats — every endured thing keeps an ember of change |
+| **Vur** → | **Syr** | heat, finished, rises — every fire ends in breath |
+| **Syr** → | **Lum** | breath, rising, carries light — every free voice wants to show |
+| **Lum** → | **Kel** | light, shown, goes far — every held light is a star not yet loosed |
+| **Kel** → | **Rav** | stars sink into night — every far promise keeps the dark that holds it |
+| **Rav** → | **Ael** | shadow, full, gathers — every night is a river of rain about to move |
+
+The marks were drawn in this order (first-flow.md §IV). The wheel is also the **year** — see below.
+
+## The Year of the Wheel
+
+One full turn of the wheel is a year. Each force keeps a *share* of the turning:
+
+| Share | Force | Name of the share |
+|-------|-------|-------------------|
+| 1 | Ael | **the Thaw** — ice loosens; the first water moves; the year remembers itself |
+| 2 | Mor | **the Sowing** — roots reach; seed breaks; kin grow |
+| 3 | Thal | **the Setting** — sap turns to heartwood; the year makes itself solid |
+| 4 | Vur | **the Ripening** — fruit heats on the stem; harvest fires; the year at full heat |
+| 5 | Syr | **the Scattering** — wind lets the fruit go; birds leave; the breath of change moves the snow |
+| 6 | Lum | **the Clearing** — light returns clear; last shadows show all; truth after harvest |
+| 7 | Kel | **the Far Night** — stars come out; the year begins to see itself from far away |
+| 8 | Rav | **the Deep** — winter sleep; dreams; seed in the dark |
+
+A year is what a turning looks like from inside the weave. A world out of wheel — a share skipped, a force silent — is a year with a missing month, and the weavers can tell which month by the shape of the grief.
+
+## The Four Crossings
+
+Beyond the wheel's hand-offs, the weave holds **four pairings** — the crossings the world loves most. A pairing is not opposition; it is the two forces that, crossed, hold a moment no single force could hold.
+
+| Pairing | The crossing they make |
+|---------|------------------------|
+| **Ael & Thal** | *the River* — motion and endurance; the most beloved crossing, and the image of the weave itself. Ael gives Thal its patience (stone remembers water); Thal gives Ael its banks (without them, flow is flood). |
+| **Vur & Rav** | *the Heart and the Sleep* — the fire in the chest and the dark behind the eyes. The inner wheel of the body: the ember cools into night; night returns the ember at waking. |
+| **Syr & Mor** | *the Breath and the Root* — the rising and the deepening of all living things. Breath feeds root; root grounds breath. Nothing lives that is not both at once. |
+| **Lum & Kel** | *the Held and the Promised* — the lamp in the hand and the stars in the sky. Lum is the light you hold; Kel is the light that holds you. The truth you speak, and the truth that speaks you. |
+
+---
+
+## The Eight
+
+### AEL — The Flow
+
+**First mark.** Drawn first, in the flow: *the flow that holds by continuing.*
+
+**Character.** Patient and restless at once. Ael never stays, and so never leaves — it simply goes. Ael keeps beginnings: everything, walked back far enough, was once a flowing. Ael does not begin things so much as *refuse to let them stop*.
+
+**Gift.** Change itself; time as life rather than measure; beginnings; the moment (*aelun*) — the one place in the flow that looks like it could be named.
+
+**Shadow.** *The Flood* — flow without banks. Everything dissolves; nothing is held. Grief washed out and never returned; a self carried past every shore it ever loved. The flood is Ael's shadow, not Ael's malice.
+
+**Crossing.** With **Thal** — the River: the weave's most beloved image. A world of Ael without Thal is flood; a world of Thal without Ael is a stone that will never know rain.
+
+**In the weave.** rivers (*sara*), rain (*nara*), the moment (*aelun*), beginnings, the sea (*saros*), the thaw.
+
+**Its voice.** long and unbroken. An Ael seal is spoken in one slow line, without pause; Ael never takes *kh* — the flow does not crack.
+
+**In the language.** prefix *ael-*; *sira* "to go", *aelav* "to flow", *aelu* "fluid, flowing".
+
+---
+
+### VUR — The Ember
+
+**First mark.** Drawn from the heart of stone: *the flow that holds by changing.*
+
+**Character.** Impatient, generous, dangerous. Vur transforms by consuming. It is the only force that *adds new thread* — a new word, a new color, a new person — by burning old thread away. The fire in the chest is Vur: anger (*vura*) and love's warmth are the same fire, told in different voices.
+
+**Gift.** Transformation; passion; renewal through destruction; the heat that makes the possible into the made.
+
+**Shadow.** *The Blaze* — burning that forgets what it was for. Wrath that consumes the weaver's own hand. The blaze does not hate; it simply stops asking *what for*, and nothing in the weave can survive a fire that no longer has a shape.
+
+**Crossing.** With **Rav** — the Heart and the Sleep: the ember cools into night, and night returns the ember at waking. Without this crossing, the chest burns forever, or never lights at all.
+
+**In the weave.** fire (*vura*), the heart, wrath, transformation, the ripening, sparks (*vurum*).
+
+**Its voice.** the only force whose seals are carried by *kh* as of right — the ember's voice, the voice of the blank sign almost made. A Vur oath is short, hot, and closed.
+
+**In the language.** prefix *vur-*; *vurav* "to burn", *vulu* "hot, fierce", *vura* "fire; anger".
+
+---
+
+### THAL — The Stone
+
+**First mark.** Drawn where roots press down: *the flow that holds by staying.*
+
+**Character.** Slow, faithful, heavy with memory. Stone is flow that agreed to stop — and Thal keeps the agreement. Thal does not resist the current; Thal *outlasts* it. Everything the world remembers, it remembers in Thal.
+
+**Gift.** Memory; the body (*thalu*); endurance; the promise that some things will still be here.
+
+**Shadow.** *The Hardening* — endurance without return. Stone that lets nothing through; memory turned to prison, keeping only the wound; a self so fixed it can no longer feel the weather. The hardening is not cruelty; it is patience with nothing left to be patient for.
+
+**Crossing.** With **Ael** — the River: stone remembers water, water shapes stone. The crossing the world uses as its own image.
+
+**In the weave.** stone (*thala*), mountains (*moru*), the body (*thalu*), the remembered, the setting.
+
+**Its voice.** one heavy syllable, said twice. A Thal seal is a weight, not a sound — you feel the seam close rather than hear it.
+
+**In the language.** prefix *th-*; *thara* "to stand, to endure", *tharina* "to remember", *thal* "solid, steadfast".
+
+---
+
+### SYR — The Breath
+
+**First mark.** Drawn from the top of a fire: *the flow that holds by leaving.*
+
+**Character.** Light, wandering, ungrasped. Syr is the voice's force — all speaking is breath first — and the thought's force: thinking is breath in the head. Syr is also the first *between*: air is the weave's original gap, the place where one thread does not touch the next.
+
+**Gift.** Freedom; the voice; thought; the spaces between things; the scattering that lets the seed find new ground.
+
+**Shadow.** *The Gale* — freedom that tears. Wind that strips the harvest; thought that cannot land; a voice that will not close, asks until the asking breaks. The gale does not hate the weave; it simply cannot hold still long enough to know what it is touching.
+
+**Crossing.** With **Mor** — the Breath and the Root: the rising and the deepening of all living things. Nothing lives that is not both at once.
+
+**In the weave.** wind (*syr*), breath, thought, the voice, the between, the scattering.
+
+**Its voice.** thin and rising. Syr is the force of questions — and a Syr seal is the only seal *left open*: no *kha*, because a question is not closed, it is let go.
+
+**In the language.** prefix *syr-*; *vora* "to speak", *syru* "free, light", *syra* "spirit".
+
+---
+
+### LUM — The Light
+
+**First mark.** Drawn where breath carries flame: *the flow that holds by showing.*
+
+**Character.** Honest, clear, warm. Lum is the lamp, the dawn, the eye. Lum is the force of truth — *lumvora*, "to speak truly", is the lit way of speaking — and of the spirit lit: a *syra* is breath, but a syra that has been shown to itself is a soul.
+
+**Gift.** Truth; seeing; spirit; blessing (*lumav*); the warmth that makes a place a home.
+
+**Shadow.** *The Glare* — light without shade. Light that shows everything shows nothing, for there is nowhere for the eye to rest. Truth spoken without mercy is Lum's shadow: a blade with the light's edge. The glare does not lie; it simply refuses to soften, and the weave is softer than any blade.
+
+**Crossing.** With **Kel** — the Held and the Promised: the lamp in the hand and the stars in the sky. Lum is the light you hold; Kel is the light that holds you.
+
+**In the weave.** light (*luma*), dawn, the eye, truth, blessings, the light-sanctuary (*luma-en*), the clearing.
+
+**Its voice.** clear and open. Lum is the force of blessings and namings — a Lum seal is spoken where everyone can hear it, because showing is what Lum does.
+
+**In the language.** prefix *lum-*; *lumav* "to bless", *luma* "light; bright", *luma-en* "light-sanctuary".
+
+---
+
+### MOR — The Root
+
+**First mark.** Drawn where the flow first nourished: *the flow that holds by reaching.*
+
+**Character.** Slow above ground, vast below. Mor's native language is kinship (*kova*) and its native act is nurture (*avel*). Mor does not rush the seed; Mor *is* the patience the seed grows into. Where Mor crosses itself, forests rise — *iluai*, the trees, are Mor reaching for Lum, and *morai*, the roots, are Mor reaching for everything else.
+
+**Gift.** Growth; kinship; seed; the mending of the weave — new thread joining old is Mor's daily work.
+
+**Shadow.** *The Overgrowth* — growth without form. Vine that strangles the tree it loves; kinship that swallows the self; love with no edges. The overgrowth is not wicked; it simply forgot that a weave needs gaps, and a forest that becomes wall is a garden that has forgotten the gate.
+
+**Crossing.** With **Syr** — the Breath and the Root. Breath feeds root; root grounds breath.
+
+**In the weave.** roots (*mora*), trees (*ilu*), the forest (*iluai*), seed, kin (*kova*), children (*tavi*), love (*avel*), the sowing.
+
+**Its voice.** low and repeated. Mor is the chant's force — its seals are spoken *twice*, because what Mor says, the weave should hear it settle.
+
+**In the language.** prefix *mor-*; *morav* "to grow", *mora* "root", *kova* "kin", *avel* "love".
+
+---
+
+### RAV — The Shadow
+
+**First mark.** Drawn last, where the stars sink: *the flow that holds by receiving.*
+
+**Character.** Soft, deep, necessary. Night is not the absence of light; it is light's shelter. The dream is the weave thinking itself over while it sleeps. Rav receives what the other seven forces set down: the heat of a fire, the shape of a day, the name of a self — and keeps it through the dark until the weave is ready for it again.
+
+**Gift.** Rest; dreams; mystery; the keeping of what is not yet nameable — seed sleeps in shadow before it breaks; an oath sleeps in shadow before it is sworn.
+
+**Shadow.** *The Long Dark* — rest without return. The dream that swallows the dreamer; the mystery that refuses, forever, to become; a night that never agrees to a dawn. The long dark is not a punishment; it is Rav holding something too long to hold.
+
+**Crossing.** With **Vur** — the Heart and the Sleep: the chest's fire and the eyes' dark, trading places with every waking.
+
+**In the weave.** night (*rav*), shadow, dreams (*dilav*), sleep (*ravav*), rest (*ravai*), sorrow's rest (*dava* lives near Rav), the deep.
+
+**Its voice.** quiet, slow, almost not said. An oath in Rav is a promise of silence; a Rav seal is whispered, because the dark does not need to be announced — only kept.
+
+**In the language.** prefix *rav-*; *ravav* "to sleep", *ravai* "to rest", *dilav* "to dream", *rav* "shadow, night".
+
+---
+
+### KEL — The Star
+
+**First mark.** Drawn where the far light keeps: *the flow that holds by promising from afar.*
+
+**Character.** Cold and exact. Fate is not cruelty; it is geometry — the stars do not choose, they simply are, and their being is far enough away to hold a shape. Kel is the only force that sees the whole weave at once, because the whole weave, seen from close, is only thread.
+
+**Gift.** Fate; distance; the far view; awe (*kela*); promise — every promise is a small Kel, a light kept burning at a distance.
+
+**Shadow.** *The Far Pull* — fate that ignores the weaver. The star that guides the ship onto the rocks, faithfully. Awe that freezes (*kela* with no movement left in it). The far pull is not the stars' cruelty; it is the cost of seeing everything — from far away, every thread looks the same length.
+
+**Crossing.** With **Lum** — the Held and the Promised: the near light and the far light, the truth you speak and the truth that speaks you.
+
+**In the weave.** stars (*keli*), the sky, fate, the far (*kelu*), the star-keepers (*kelakar*), awe (*kela*), the far night.
+
+**Its voice.** high and still. A Kel seal is spoken after a full breath of silence — the star speaks only when the world has stopped talking to itself.
+
+**In the language.** prefix *kel-*; *keli* "star", *kelai* "stars", *kela* "awe", *kelu* "far", *kelakar* "star-keeper".
+
+---
+
+## Balance & the Thin Places
+
+The weave needs all eight. A world missing one force is a weave with a missing thread, and where the thread is missing the weave is thin — a **thin place**. At a thin place the world can be seen through:
+
+- A world without **Ael** is a stone that will never know rain.
+- A world without **Vur** keeps its shape forever and never learns a new one.
+- A world without **Thal** flows so fast nothing can be held to be remembered.
+- A world without **Syr** has no voice, no gap, no between — only pressed-together thread.
+- A world without **Lum** is the weave in the dark, true but unshowable.
+- A world without **Mor** has no growing, no kin, no mending — fray after fray, never joined.
+- A world without **Rav** never sleeps, and a weave that never sleeps frays in its own seeing.
+- A world without **Kel** has no far, no promise, no fate — only the thread immediately at hand.
+
+The weavers' answer to a thin place is a **blessing under the missing force** — *lumav* for a world that has lost its light, *morav morav* for a fray that will not join. (Full ceremonial forms: planned for `04-culture/ceremonies/`.)
+
+## The Voices of the Forces — Ritual Table
+
+| Force | Manner of speech | The seal |
+|-------|------------------|----------|
+| Ael | long, unbroken line | one slow line, no pause, never *kh* |
+| Vur | short, hot | always *kh*-carried — the ember's voice |
+| Thal | one heavy syllable | said twice; a weight, not a sound |
+| Syr | thin, rising | left open — no *kha*; a question let go |
+| Lum | clear, open | spoken where all can hear |
+| Mor | low, repeated | said twice, to let it settle |
+| Rav | quiet, slow | whispered; the dark kept, not announced |
+| Kel | high, still | after a full breath of silence |
+
+## Summary
+
+| Force | Name | Holds by | Domains | Shadow | Crossing |
+|-------|------|----------|---------|--------|----------|
+| `ael-` | Ael | continuing | water, time, change, beginnings | the Flood | Thal — the River |
+| `vur-` | Vur | changing | fire, passion, transformation, wrath | the Blaze | Rav — the Heart and the Sleep |
+| `th-`  | Thal | staying | earth, endurance, memory, body | the Hardening | Ael — the River |
+| `syr-` | Syr | leaving | wind, thought, freedom, voice | the Gale | Mor — the Breath and the Root |
+| `lum-` | Lum | showing | light, truth, spirit, blessing | the Glare | Kel — the Held and the Promised |
+| `mor-` | Mor | reaching | growth, kinship, nurture, seed | the Overgrowth | Syr — the Breath and the Root |
+| `rav-` | Rav | receiving | dream, rest, mystery, night | the Long Dark | Vur — the Heart and the Sleep |
+| `kel-` | Kel | promising from afar | fate, distance, cosmos, awe | the Far Pull | Lum — the Held and the Promised |
