+# The LinKod Codex
+
+The complete symbolic system: foundations, language, computation, and culture.
+
+```
+codex/
+├── 01-foundations/    Mythic foundations — the First Flow, the Eight Sacred Forces,
+│                      mythic entities, realms & cosmology, ritual theory
+├── 02-language/       The linguistic core
+│   ├── grammar.md     Core grammar: phonology, morphology, syntax, ritual syntax
+│   ├── dictionary.md  Starter dictionary (~80 entries)
+│   └── lexicon/       Thematic lexicons: nature, emotion, social, technology, mythic
+├── 03-computation/    Symbolic & computational tools — interpreter blueprint,
+│                      formal ritual-syntax spec, example LinKod programs
+└── 04-culture/        Myths, ritual chants, ceremonies, storytelling structures,
+                       glyphs & calligraphy (Kod-script)
+```
+
+## Reading order
+
+1. `02-language/grammar.md` — start here; it is self-contained and includes a condensed force table and worked examples.
+2. `02-language/dictionary.md` — the working wordlist.
+3. `01-foundations/` — once written, it supplies the cosmology the grammar's force system refers to.
+4. `03-computation/` — how the grammar maps onto the LinKod interpreter.
+5. `04-culture/` — the living text: myths, chants, ceremonies, and the glyph script.
+
